### Third-Party Notices & Acknowledgments

This project builds upon, interacts with, and references several upstream open-source components, fonts, and community research. Respective copyrights and licenses apply:

- **OpenBSD Project**:
  - Copyright (c) 1982-2026 The Regents of the University of California, Theo de Raadt, and contributors.
  - `configs/install.md` incorporates logic from OpenBSD's installer scripts:
    Copyright (c) 1996 Canonical Software. All rights reserved.
    Redistribution and use in source and binary forms are permitted under standard BSD/ISC terms.
  - OpenBSD kernel source modifications (`scripts/patches/dwc2_split_order_fix.patch` and `scripts/patches/gpiokeys_rawkbd_fix.patch`) are distributed under the ISC License.
  - OpenBSD base distribution sets (`base79.tgz`, `bsd.rd`, etc.) and packages are downloaded from official OpenBSD mirrors under ISC / BSD licenses.
  - https://www.openbsd.org/

- **Joshua Stein (jcs)**:
  - Custom DM250 OpenBSD kernel patches, U-Boot, and device tree (DTB) support:
    https://jcs.org/2026/04/09/openbsd-dm250
    Binaries and scripts are fetched from upstream sources during installation under respective ISC / GPL licenses.
  - Wi-Fi NVRAM configuration parameter template for Broadcom AP6212 / BCM43430 (`configs/brcmfmac43430-sdio.rockchip,pomera-dm250.txt`).

- **4noha**:
  - Research, kernel patches (`scripts/patches/bcmbt_delay_2s.patch`, `scripts/patches/rkdrm_wsdisplay_smode.patch` under the ISC License), mlterm-fb patches (`scripts/patches/mlterm-fb-dm250-shadowfb.patch` and `scripts/patches/mlterm-fb-dm250-optimized.patch` under the MIT License), Bluetooth PAN tethering research, and power management concepts for Pomera DM250:
    Copyright (c) 2026 4noha
    https://github.com/4noha/openbsd-pomera-dm250

- **mlterm (ARAKI Ken)**:
  - Multilingual terminal emulator (`mlterm`):
    Copyright (c) 2000-2026 ARAKI Ken. All rights reserved.
    Distributed under the BSD-style License. Source code and packages are fetched dynamically during build:
    https://github.com/arakiken/mlterm / https://mlterm.sourceforge.net/

- **ichinomoto**:
  - Pioneering research on Pomera DM200 / DM250 Linux (Debian) bring-up, hardware reverse engineering, and safe eMMC backup methodologies:
    https://www.ekesete.net/log/?p=9504

- **Typography & Font Resources**:
  - **UDEV Gothic** (supported in `scripts/pomera-font.sh`):
    Copyright (c) 2022-2026 yuru7.
    Distributed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
    Derived from BIZ UD Gothic (TypeBank / Morisawa Inc. & Google LLC, OFL 1.1) and JetBrains Mono (JetBrains s.r.o., Apache 2.0).
    https://github.com/yuru7/udev-gothic
  - **Moralerspace** (supported in `scripts/pomera-font.sh`):
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 yuru7.
    Distributed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
    Derived from Monaspace (GitHub, Inc., OFL 1.1) and BIZ UD Gothic (TypeBank / Morisawa Inc. & Google LLC, OFL 1.1).
    https://github.com/yuru7/moralerspace
  - **Noto Sans CJK / Noto Sans Mono CJK JP** (configured in `scripts/pomera-setup-workspace.sh`):
    Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Google LLC.
    Distributed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
    Installed via the official OpenBSD package `noto-cjk`.
    https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk

- **Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.**:
  - Bootloader miniloader and DDR initialization binaries (`rkbin`) are fetched directly from Rockchip's official repositories under Rockchip binary license terms.

